# Keys whose baseline is not what the reader produces when nothing is written.
# Regenerate with -update.
#
# A row means a node with this key missing runs the absent value today and would run
# the baseline once the section is declared. Guarding the read is what empties this
# file: the absent column then becomes the declared default and the row disappears.
#
# A row compares two values and not what the reader does with them, so some rows are a
# difference in how a value is written rather than in what a node runs: "" and "0" are
# the same number to a reader that casts. Read the pair before treating a row as a change.
#
# key	setting	absent	baseline	modes

state-commit.sc-enable	Enable	false	true	all
